## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to implement streaming statistics with efficient data structures and real-time median calculation.

## Key Concepts

- Dual heap structure (max-heap + min-heap)
- Balance invariant maintenance
- Median computation in O(log n) per insert
- Streaming data processing

## Code Example

```javascript
class MedianStream {
  constructor() {
    this.low = new MaxHeap();  // Lower half
    this.high = new MinHeap(); // Upper half
  }

  insert(x) {
    // Insert into appropriate heap and rebalance
    if (this.low.isEmpty() || x <= this.low.peek()) {
      this.low.push(x);
    } else {
      this.high.push(x);
    }

    // Rebalance to maintain size difference ≤ 1
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size() + 1) {
      this.high.push(this.low.pop());
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size() + 1) {
      this.low.push(this.high.pop());
    }
  }

  getMedian() {
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size()) {
      return this.low.peek();
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size()) {
      return this.high.peek();
    } else {
      return (this.low.peek() + this.high.peek()) / 2;
    }
  }
}
```

## Implementation Notes

- Duplicates are handled naturally by heap properties
- Memory usage is O(n) for storing all elements
- Suitable for real-time streaming applications
- Can be extended to support removal operations with additional bookkeeping

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical string data-struct understanding: duplicates, memory use, and prefix-based queries via a Trie vs simpler maps.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node passCount and endCount
- Duplicate handling via endCount; memory managed by lazy pruning
- Time complexity O(|word|) insert/delete and O(|prefix|) query

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.pass = 0;
    this.end = 0;
  }
}

class WordDict {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    node.pass++;
    for (const ch of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(ch)) node.children.set(ch, new TrieNode());
      node = node.children.get(ch);
      node.pass++;
    }
    node.end++;
  }
  delete(word) {
    if (!this._exists(word)) return false;
    let node = this.root;
    node.pass--;
    for (const ch of word) {
      const next = node.children.get(ch);
      next.pass--;
      if (next.pass === 0) { node.children.delete(ch); return true; }
      node = next;
    }
    node.end--;
    return true;
  }
  countPrefix(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(ch)) return 0;
      node = node.children.get(ch);
    }
    return node.pass;
  }
  _exists(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(ch)) return false;
      node = node.children.get(ch);
    }
    return node.end > 0;
  }
}
```

